scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:824:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-1979-5-2,commonlii-LKSC-1979-5,(1995) 1 Sri LR 7,LKSC,1979,"The draft deed of transfer was received by 1st defendant four days prior to the date fixed for signing the transfer. There was no uncertainty in relation to the vendors and vendee, the subject matter of the sale and the consideration. There was sufficient compliance on the part of the plaintiff in regard to the stipulation, of notice of the, draft. Although a plaintiff who breaks-an-essential term of the agreement cannot claim specific performance, trivial breaches do not disentitle a party from claiming relief","(1) The 1st defendant had held himself out as the agent of the other defendants and the other defendants by their own conduct held out that the 1st defendant was their sole spokesman in relation to the transaction so much as to induce Gnanam, Managing Director of the plaintiff company and the lawyers for the company that the 1st defendant was a sufficient medium through which notice could reach the other defendants. The 1st defendant did not give evidence and the court is entitled to draw the presumption that had he given evidence; such evidence would have been unfavourable to the case of the defendants - see section 114 illustration (f) of the Evidence Ordinance. (2) The draft deed of transfer was received by 1st defendant four days prior to the date fixed for signing the transfer. There was no uncertainty in relation to the vendors and vendee, the subject matter of the sale and the consideration. There was sufficient compliance on the part of the plaintiff in regard to the stipulation, of notice of the, draft. Although a plaintiff who breaks-an-essential term of the agreement cannot claim specific performance, trivial breaches do not disentitle a party from claiming relief. (3) Time was of the essence of the contract only in respect of the last date for signing the deed of transfer and in no other respect On the last date for signing, the defendants were not available and wanted a further date to sign the deed of transfer. 8 (4) The plaintiff was entitled to a decree for specific performance",SRC029-s114,none,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:825:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-1979-5-3,commonlii-LKSC-1979-5,(1995) 1 Sri LR 7,LKSC,1979,"Time was of the essence of the contract only in respect of the last date for signing the deed of transfer and in no other respect On the last date for signing, the defendants were not available and wanted a further date to sign the deed of transfer. 8","(1) The 1st defendant had held himself out as the agent of the other defendants and the other defendants by their own conduct held out that the 1st defendant was their sole spokesman in relation to the transaction so much as to induce Gnanam, Managing Director of the plaintiff company and the lawyers for the company that the 1st defendant was a sufficient medium through which notice could reach the other defendants. The 1st defendant did not give evidence and the court is entitled to draw the presumption that had he given evidence; such evidence would have been unfavourable to the case of the defendants - see section 114 illustration (f) of the Evidence Ordinance. (2) The draft deed of transfer was received by 1st defendant four days prior to the date fixed for signing the transfer. There was no uncertainty in relation to the vendors and vendee, the subject matter of the sale and the consideration. There was sufficient compliance on the part of the plaintiff in regard to the stipulation, of notice of the, draft. Although a plaintiff who breaks-an-essential term of the agreement cannot claim specific performance, trivial breaches do not disentitle a party from claiming relief. (3) Time was of the essence of the contract only in respect of the last date for signing the deed of transfer and in no other respect On the last date for signing, the defendants were not available and wanted a further date to sign the deed of transfer. 8 (4) The plaintiff was entitled to a decree for specific performance",SRC029-s114,none,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:1532:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_appeal_120_2012.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_appeal_120_2012.pdf,,SC,2012,Prescription begins to run from the date of the demand in an overdraft case.,"In the present case, prescription begins to run from the date of the demand.",SRC071-s7,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:1647:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_appeal_15_2008.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_appeal_15_2008.pdf,,SC,2008,"A court may presume the existence of any fact which it thinks likely to have happened, regard being had to the common course of natural events, human conduct, and public and private business in their relation to the facts of the particular case – that judicial and official acts have been regularly performed.",This evidence contained in the affidavit has not been challenged either by raising an issue on this matter or calling the Fiscal Officer who executed the writ and eliciting the fact that possession had not been handed over as claimed by the Appellant. No independent evidence was led to rebut this presumption.,SRC029-s114(d),bad-source,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:1741:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_appeal_1_2016.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_appeal_1_2016.pdf,,SC,2016,A document marked 'P3' without objection at the closure of the case is deemed to be admitted as evidence.,"Therefore, at this juncture, the document marked ‘P3’ ought to be admitted as evidence for all purposes of law considering the fact that no objection was taken at the closure of the Plaintiffs-Appellants case.",SRC029-s114,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:1803:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_appeal_29_2009.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_appeal_29_2009.pdf,,SC,2009,"A creditor who entered into a settlement in a Debt Conciliation Board in which a conditional transfer figured, is not prevented from later instituting a vindicatory action claiming title based on that conditional transfer.",I do not see that there can be any disability for the plaintiff to bring an action upon the title he had obtained by the deed of transfer in his favour upon the footing that there had been a default resulting in the right to redeem having come to an end.,SRC001-s43,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:1821:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_appeal_32_2021.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_appeal_32_2021.pdf,,SC,2021,A party cannot take up new positions which are questions of fact for the first time on appeal.,The defendants cannot take up new positions which are questions of fact for the first time on appeal.,SRC029-s114,none,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:1864:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_appeal_43_2012.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_appeal_43_2012.pdf,,SC,2012,"The word 'owner' in Section 40 of the Forest Ordinance should be given a purposive interpretation, considering the intention of the legislature.",In my view the word “owner” as it occurs in Section 40 of the Forest Ordinance cannot be considered in isolation applying purely legal definition of the term “owner” but must be given a purposive interpretation taking into account the intention of the legislature.,SRC001-s40,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:2102:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_29_2011.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_29_2011.pdf,,SC,2011,An unwritten promise or agreement between parties is enforceable if the action is commenced within three years from the time the cause of action arose.,"I hold according to the evidence placed by documents before court that there was an unwritten promise/bargain between the parties with regard to payments for the advertisements and programs telecast after 2004 December. The cause of action to recover the dues had arisen in June, 2005 and action had been filed in September, 2006 which is within 3 years from the date of the cause of action.",SRC071-s7,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:2129:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_7_2012.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_7_2012.pdf,,SC,2012,An action to recover a debt based on an account stated is not prescribed within three years.,An action to recover the balance was prescribed in three years.,SRC071-s7,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:2137:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_fr_13_2020.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_fr_13_2020.pdf,,SC,2020,"A person who has agreed to purchase a house on an installment basis can be considered as having a main document in proof of residence, and is entitled to obtain full marks for that document.","When considering the totality of the evidence placed before this Court, I hold that the 1st Petitioner is entitled to obtain full marks to the document produce marked as 9A, the main document in proof of the Residence of the Petitioner.",SRC001-s4,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:2156:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_fr_311_2016-1.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_fr_311_2016-1.pdf,,SC,2016,A public officer cannot be transferred due to service exigencies at the whims and fancies of a superior.,"Moreover, a public officer cannot be transferred due to service exigencies at the whims and fancies of a superior.",SRC029-s114(f),none,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:2193:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_rule_3_2011.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_rule_3_2011.pdf,,SC,2011,"A practicing attorney-at-law and notary public who is convicted of serious offenses, including forgery and fraud, and receives a light sentence, may be suspended from practicing their profession for a period of time.","It is unimaginable that the original records and files maintained by the High Court of Colombo and the Attorney General’s Department, which are the primary institutions involved in law enforcement, could be made to disappear so easily.",SRC014-s19(2),bad-source,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
