scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules_high_confidence.csv:1176:draftly-rule-courts-coa-CA-PHC-124-22-Judgment-Final.pdf-1,courts-coa-CA-PHC-124-22-Judgment-Final.pdf,,COA,,The lessor retains proprietary rights in the leased equipment and is entitled to recover possession upon default.,"Under the Leasing Act, a finance lease is an arrangement whereby possession and use of equipment are transferred to the lessee while ownership remains vested in the lessor.",SRC001-s15,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
