scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:2097:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_24_2008.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_24_2008.pdf,,SC,2008,"A contract of suretyship is in essence a contract by which one person, the surety, agrees to answer for some existing or future liability of another, the principal (or principal debtor), to a third party, the creditor, and by which the surety’s liability is in addition to, and not in substitution for, the liability of the principal.","A contract of suretyship is in essence a contract by which one person, the surety, agrees to answer for some existing or future liability of another, the principal (or principal debtor), to a third party, the creditor, and by which the surety’s liability is in addition to, and not in substitution for, the liability of the principal.",SRC029-s101,none,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:2102:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_29_2011.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_29_2011.pdf,,SC,2011,An unwritten promise or agreement between parties is enforceable if the action is commenced within three years from the time the cause of action arose.,"I hold according to the evidence placed by documents before court that there was an unwritten promise/bargain between the parties with regard to payments for the advertisements and programs telecast after 2004 December. The cause of action to recover the dues had arisen in June, 2005 and action had been filed in September, 2006 which is within 3 years from the date of the cause of action.",SRC071-s7,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
