scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:2110:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_3_2009.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_3_2009.pdf,,SC,2009,An action based on a written contract is not prescribed if brought within six years from the date of the breach of such contract.,"Section 6 of the Prescription Ordinance provides that; “No action shall be maintainable upon ... any written promise, contract, bargain, or agreement, ... unless such action shall be brought within six years from the date of the breach of such ... contract, bargain or agreement, ... from the date when such note or bill shall have become due, or of the last payment of interest thereon.”",SRC071-s6,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
