scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:2193:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_rule_3_2011.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_rule_3_2011.pdf,,SC,2011,"A practicing attorney-at-law and notary public who is convicted of serious offenses, including forgery and fraud, and receives a light sentence, may be suspended from practicing their profession for a period of time.","It is unimaginable that the original records and files maintained by the High Court of Colombo and the Attorney General’s Department, which are the primary institutions involved in law enforcement, could be made to disappear so easily.",SRC014-s19(2),bad-source,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:2197:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_rule_5_2023.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_rule_5_2023.pdf,,SC,2023,An attorney-at-law must exercise their skill with due diligence to the best of their ability and care in the interest of their client.,"by reason of the aforesaid acts and conduct, you have not exercised your skill with due diligence to the best of your ability and care in the interest of your client and have thus committed the breach of Rule 15 of the Supreme Court (Conduct of and Etiquette for Attorneys-at-Law) Rules 1988,",SRC014-s26(b),bad-source,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
