scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_high_confidence.csv:1148:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_balapitiya_830_98.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_balapitiya_830_98.pdf,,COA,,The burden of proof rests squarely and fairly on a party invoking the provisions of Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance to defeat the ownership of an adverse claimant to immovable property to establish a starting point for their acquisition of prescriptive rights.,"Where a party invokes the provisions of Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance in order to defeat the ownership of an adverse claimant to immovable property, the burden of proof rests squarely and fairly on him to establish a starting point for his or her acquisition of prescriptive rights.",SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance,True,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
