scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_high_confidence.csv:1527:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_fr_13_2020.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_fr_13_2020.pdf,,SC,2020,A person who has agreed to purchase a house on an installment basis can use the agreement as proof of residence.,"When considering the totality of the evidence placed before this Court, I hold that the 1st Petitioner is entitled to obtain full marks to the document produce marked as 9A, the main document in proof of the Residence of the Petitioner.",SRC001-s4,none,,False,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_high_confidence.csv:1534:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_fr_311_2016-1.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_fr_311_2016-1.pdf,,SC,2016,A public officer's transfer must be based on a valid reason and the officer must be made aware of the reason.,"The PSC Rules recognise three different categories of exigencies of service, so merely stating that it was on exigencies of service is not sufficient.",SRC029-s114(f),none,Article 12 (1) of the Constitution,True,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_high_confidence.csv:1540:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_rule_3_2011.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_rule_3_2011.pdf,,SC,2011,"A practicing attorney-at-law and notary public who has been convicted of serious offenses, including forgery and fraud, and has received a light sentence, may be suspended from practicing his profession for a period of eight years.","It is unimaginable that the original records and files maintained by the High Court of Colombo and the Attorney General’s Department, which are the primary institutions involved in law enforcement, could be made to disappear so easily.",SRC014-s19(2),bad-source,"Section 42(2) of the Judicature Act No. 2 of 1978, Section 30(12) and Section 39 of the Notaries Ordinance No. 1 of 1907, as subsequently amended, Rule 60 and 61 of the Supreme Court (Conduct of and Etiquette for Attorney-at-Law) Rules 1988",False,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
